Dual-use capability disclosure

This software is intended for a user to analyse a WeChat group that they are
authorised to access on their own Windows computer. When the user explicitly
configures a group and starts a sync (or opts in to automatic sync), the
history reader scans a running WeChat process for database encryption keys,
makes local snapshots and temporarily decrypts database copies. Those copies
can contain conversations other than the selected group. Only the configured
group is imported by the supported wrapper.

The wrapper does not intentionally persist extracted keys, disables the
upstream key-cache routines, and restricts the history worker's Python socket
operations. Temporary plaintext lives under the selected data directory and
may remain after forced termination or a crash. Other local processes can
access data according to the operating system's file and process permissions.
The local MCP interface can expose retrieved content to the client, and a
cloud-connected client may transmit it to a remote service.

The included third-party source module contains additional upstream functions
and should not be called directly expecting the wrapper's restrictions. Do not
use this software to access another person's device, account, keys or messages
without their authorisation. See README.md for setup, limitations and the
third-party license and attribution.
